            <ArticleTitle>Resolution of bony metastases after bilateral orchiectomy for carcinoma of prostate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>353-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Resolution of multiple bony metastases after bilateral orchiectomy for carcinoma of prostate was documented by roentgenogram and scintigraphy. This marked improvement was correlated with a decline in serum acid phosphatase, disappearance of soft tissue tumor, and clinical improvement in the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
